We are looking for a Head of Compliance & Customer Protection to join our team.
Your main tasks will be:
Merge moderation and Customer Protection into one process: signal → risk assessment → review → decision → enforcement → appeal;
Manage moderation of clients and partners: set review priorities, SLAs, quality control and the review of wrongful restrictions;
Run investigations of complaints and violations: fraud, pressure on clients and other prohibited practices; ensure evidence and proportionate decisions;
Develop and update rules together with Legal; turn agreed requirements into instructions for moderators, Support, Supply and partners;
Ensure decisions are enforced across teams: Support communicates with the client, Supply drives partner actions, Compliance checks that the violation is fixed and does not recur;
Remove root causes of repeat violations: change checks, rules, partner training and product requirements based on investigation findings;
Automate checks with error control: together with ML and automation, choose processes to automate and set requirements for accuracy, manual review, appeals and rollback;
Manage the team (in-house and freelancers) and the function's efficiency: plan workload, train people, review errors, control the speed, quality and cost of checks;
Report the risk picture: serious and repeat violations, misses, wrongful blocks, investigation timelines and enforcement of measures.
We expect from you:
Building an end-to-end risk process: intake, risk assessment, investigation, decision, enforcement, appeal;
Moderation management: priorities, SLAs, quality control, sample-based review;
Investigations: collecting evidence, recognising fraud and pressure patterns, proportionate measures;
Turning legal requirements into operational rules and instructions for several teams;
Automating checks with ML: requirements for accuracy, manual review, appeals and rollback; evaluating pilots by missed violations and wrongful blocks;
Data and reporting: case tracking by risk, cause, timing, decisions and recurrence; checking data quality and separating the effect of measures from changes in volume.
What do we offer:
REMOTE OPPORTUNITY to work full-time;
